# Game Life

I want my life running with projects, the habits are not the main part but a subbranch of projects. For example, I want 100 kg at bench press. So the app will show me the deadline and I'll gain xp, stuffs with each steps done. I want the app to be able to receive photos and videos and I can then watch them on the app. I don't want my character to move in the game, just me with my stuffs.

Project : 100 kg bench press/ 100 kg deadlift/ 100 kg squat.

Deadline : 31 december

Right now : 65 kg bench press/ 60 kg deadlift/ 60 kg squat

Xp : 50 xp every +5 kgs in any exercises
    100 xp every +10 kgs.
I mean every dizaine is 100 xp.

Habits : gym everyday, I don't know when I'll need rest.
Every streak week is 150 xp. Always put a photo proof.
----
import { kgToGo } from "./rules.js";
import {load } from "../js/storage.js"

const state = load();

function render(){
    document.getElementById("nickname").textContent = state.nickname;
    document.getElementById("level").textContent = `Level : ${state.level}`;
    document.getElementById("xp").textContent = `${state.xp} / ${state.xpNeed}`;
}

render();----
const state = {
    player : "Arthurooo",
    nickname : "loser",
    level : 1,
    xp : 0,
    xpNeed : 100,
    projects : [],
};

export function save(state){
    const text = JSON.stringify(state);
    localStorage.setItem("Current State", text);
}

export function load(){
    const saved = localStorage.getItem("Current State");
    if (saved){
        return JSON.parse(saved);
    }
    else{
        return state;
    }
}----
export function kgToGo(current, target)
{
    let count = target - current;
    if (current >= target)
        count = 0;
    if (count > target)
        count = "Error";
    return (count);
}

export function percentDone(current, target)
{
    let percent = current / target * 100;
}

export function formatLevel(lvl, current, target)
{
    let count = kgToGo(current, target);
    return (`Level ${lvl} : ${count}/100`);
}
